      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-42347",
      ":question/problem": "An enterprise has $30$ workers of different nationalities. There are $5$ workers who have dual Venezuelan and American citizenship, $12$ workers who have Venezuelan citizenship, and $21$ workers who have American citizenship.\n\nIf $A$ represents the event that a worker has Venezuelan citizenship, and $B$ represents the event that a worker has American citizenship, which of the following diagrams gives the correct Venn diagram for the corresponding sample space?"
